<?xml version='1.0' standalone='yes'?>
<!DOCTYPE PLUGIN [
  <!ENTITY name "md12xx.fancontrol">
  <!ENTITY author "TheIlluminate92">
  <!ENTITY version "0.4.2">
  <!ENTITY launch "MD12xxFanControl">
]>

<PLUGIN name="&name;" author="&author;" version="&version;" launch="&launch;" pluginURL="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/TheIlluminate92/unraid-md12xx-fan-control/main/releases/md12xx.fancontrol.plg" min="6.12.0" support="https://github.com/TheIlluminate92/unraid-md12xx-fan-control/issues" icon="fan">
<CHANGES>
### 0.4.2 Beta
- Disables serial adapters already selected by another shelf immediately, without a page refresh.

### 0.4.1 Beta
- Uses Unraid's stock Disk Settings icon metadata for a reliable Settings tile across themes.
- Makes the Auto curve point count resize after typing or changing the requested count.
- Makes Refresh discovery save only discovery options and run one guarded pass immediately.
- Shows controller fault details, target reasons, telemetry state, and command state in the app.
- Prevents duplicate hardware assignments and blocks configuration or control writes during Identify &amp; test.
- Stops tests safely during update/uninstall and avoids rebuilding the form from completed jobs.
- Fixes archive downloads, strengthens diagnostic redaction, and hardens inline configuration encoding.
- Saves commissioning RPM calibration, verifies later commands against SES telemetry, and detects response drift.
- Uses fail-safe speed for incomplete or changed disk mappings and recovers stale commissioning locks.
- Keeps Settings open while downloading local diagnostic and test archives.

### 0.4.0 Beta
- Adds fully app-driven Identify &amp; test with live progress and safe server-side continuation.
- Adds a packaged Settings icon and fixes shelf-name editing so refreshes do not steal focus.
- Uses generic competing-controller messages and reports blocked shelf writes accurately.
- Lowers hardware telemetry polling to 5 seconds while saved control changes remain immediate.
- Removes installation-specific wording from the public interface and documentation.

### 0.3.0 Beta
- Adds Manual speeds from 20% through 100% in 10% increments.
- Turns off active FTDI testing automatically after setup; passive inventory remains available.
- Makes uninstall a complete reset that removes persistent configuration and commissioning results.
- Adds expandable setup help, clearer disk mappings, a 2–10 point stacked Auto curve, and local redacted diagnostics.
- Adds Community Apps metadata, hardware-report forms, privacy/security documentation, and generic MD1220 test coverage.
- MD1200 is hardware-tested; MD1220 and additional HBA/firmware reports are requested.

### 0.2.3
- Uses the hardware-proven reader-first serial session for every speed command.
- Requires independent SES RPM proof of the final 20% restoration before commissioning succeeds.

### 0.2.2
- Maps disks through the verified SES device's SAS expander when enclosure-class links are unavailable.
- Prevents discovery from racing the commissioning test's final 20% safety restore.

### 0.2.1
- Fixes BlueDress speed writes by keeping the serial console open read/write and consuming its replies.

### 0.2.0
- Adds RPM-proven automatic serial-to-SES identification and automatic Unraid disk assignment.
- Keeps a manual mapping fallback and refuses ambiguous or empty automatic mappings.

### 0.1.3
- Fixes the blank Unraid Settings page caused by page-builder path resolution.

### 0.1.2
- Moves updates and support to the dedicated standalone repository.

### 0.1.1
- Validates conservative discovery against mixed USB serial and SES hardware.
- Fixes the controller startup parser and adds an installation banner.

### 0.1.0
- Initial standalone beta for Dell PowerVault MD1200 and MD1220 shelves.
- Adds multi-shelf configuration, conservative background discovery, Auto/Manual control, independent RPM telemetry, locking, and guarded commissioning.
- Optional serial verification is read-only, requires an MD12xx-shaped `_who` response, and is blocked while another fan controller is active.
</CHANGES>

<FILE Run="/bin/bash">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
set -e
RUNTIME_DIR="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol"
CONFIG_DIR="/boot/config/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol"

if [ -x "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stop.sh" ]; then
  "$RUNTIME_DIR/scripts/stop.sh"
fi
rm -rf "$RUNTIME_DIR"
mkdir -p "$RUNTIME_DIR" "$CONFIG_DIR"
]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>

<FILE Name="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/md12xx.fancontrol/assets/css/settings.css">
<INLINE>
<![CDATA[
.md12xx-page { max-width: 1180px; margin: 18px auto 40px; color: var(--text-color, #ddd); }
.md12xx-hero, .md12xx-title-row, .md12xx-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 16px; }
.md12xx-hero-actions { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
.md12xx-hero h2, .md12xx-panel h3 { margin: 0; }
.md12xx-hero p { margin: 5px 0 0; opacity: .72; }
.md12xx-beta { margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 10px 12px; color: #ffd166; background: rgba(255,209,102,.08); border-left: 3px solid #ffd166; }
.md12xx-controller-detail { margin: 12px 0 0; padding: 10px 12px; color: #ffb3b3; background: rgba(255,107,107,.08); border-left: 3px solid #ff6b6b; }
.md12xx-controller-detail.is-attention { color: #ffd166; background: rgba(255,209,102,.08); border-left-color: #ffd166; }
.md12xx-help { margin-top: 12px; }
.md12xx-help ol { margin: 14px 0 0 22px; padding: 0; line-height: 1.55; }
.md12xx-help li + li { margin-top: 7px; }
.md12xx-panel { margin-top: 16px; padding: 18px; background: #17191c; border: 1px solid #33383e; border-radius: 4px; }
.md12xx-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(190px, 1fr)); gap: 14px 18px; margin-top: 15px; }
.md12xx-grid label, .md12xx-shelf label { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; }
.md12xx-grid small, .md12xx-shelf small { opacity: .65; }
.md12xx-page input, .md12xx-page select { box-sizing: border-box; min-height: 34px; padding: 6px 9px; color: #eee; background: #0e1012; border: 1px solid #424850; }
.md12xx-page input[type="checkbox"] { width: 22px; min-height: 22px; }
.md12xx-page button { padding: 8px 14px; color: #f2f2f2; background: #292e34; border: 1px solid #555d66; cursor: pointer; }
.md12xx-page button:hover { border-color: #f15a2b; }
.md12xx-page .md12xx-primary { background: #cf4a20; border-color: #f15a2b; }
.md12xx-pill { padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 12px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: .08em; background: #343a40; }
.md12xx-pill.is-normal { color: #70df9b; }.md12xx-pill.is-attention { color: #ffd166; }.md12xx-pill.is-fault { color: #ff6b6b; }
.md12xx-message { margin-top: 14px; padding: 11px 13px; border-left: 3px solid #f15a2b; background: #24282d; }
.md12xx-warning { margin: 16px 0 0; color: #ffd166; }
.md12xx-discovery-summary { margin: 14px 0 0; padding: 10px 12px; border-left: 3px solid #4bb3fd; background: rgba(75,179,253,.08); }
.md12xx-shelf { margin-top: 14px; padding: 14px; border: 1px solid #343a40; background: #111316; }
.md12xx-shelf-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; gap: 12px; margin-bottom: 12px; }
.md12xx-shelf-head strong { font-size: 15px; }
.md12xx-shelf-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(260px, 1fr)); gap: 13px 18px; }
.md12xx-shelf .md12xx-disks { min-height: 120px; }
.md12xx-manual { margin-top: 12px; border: 1px solid #343a40; padding: 10px 12px; background: #0d0f11; }
.md12xx-manual summary { cursor: pointer; color: #f4b942; font-weight: 600; }
.md12xx-manual[open] summary { margin-bottom: 12px; }
.md12xx-assignment-summary { line-height: 1.45; }
.md12xx-mapped-disks { margin-top: 12px; padding: 10px 12px; background: rgba(75,179,253,.08); border-left: 3px solid #4bb3fd; line-height: 1.45; }
.md12xx-mapped-disks strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 3px; }
.md12xx-status { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(120px, 1fr)); gap: 8px; margin-top: 12px; }
.md12xx-status span { padding: 8px; background: #1c2024; font-size: 12px; }
.md12xx-status b { display: block; margin-top: 3px; font-size: 15px; }
.md12xx-commission { margin-top: 12px; padding: 12px; background: #090a0b; border: 1px solid #343a40; }
.md12xx-commission-head { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; }
.md12xx-commission p { margin: 9px 0 0; opacity: .72; line-height: 1.4; }
.md12xx-commission-phase { font-size: 12px; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .06em; }
.md12xx-commission-phase.is-running { color: #4bb3fd; }
.md12xx-commission-phase.is-passed { color: #70df9b; }
.md12xx-commission-phase.is-failed { color: #ff6b6b; }
.md12xx-commission-output { max-height: 250px; margin: 12px 0 0; padding: 10px; overflow: auto; white-space: pre-wrap; color: #d9e0e6; background: #050607; border: 1px solid #2d3238; font: 12px/1.45 monospace; }
.md12xx-commission-result { display: inline-block; margin-top: 10px; color: #4bb3fd; }
.md12xx-commission-result[hidden] { display: none; }
.md12xx-page button:disabled { cursor: not-allowed; opacity: .5; }
.md12xx-point-count { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }.md12xx-point-count input { width: 72px; }
.md12xx-curve { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(var(--md12xx-curve-columns, 4), minmax(110px, 1fr)); gap: 12px; margin-top: 14px; }
.md12xx-curve-step { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; padding: 10px; background: #111316; border: 1px solid #343a40; }
.md12xx-curve-step label { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 5px; }
.md12xx-inline { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin-top: 14px; }.md12xx-inline input { width: 90px; }
.md12xx-actions { margin-top: 18px; justify-content: flex-end; }
@media (max-width: 850px) { .md12xx-grid, .md12xx-shelf-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }.md12xx-curve { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }.md12xx-status { grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); }.md12xx-title-row { align-items: flex-start; }.md12xx-hero { align-items: flex-start; }.md12xx-hero-actions { flex-direction: column-reverse; align-items: flex-end; } }

]]>
</INLINE>
</FILE>
